<title>USA: Herman Miller Inc Q3 March 1 net rises.</title>
<headline>Herman Miller Inc Q3 March 1 net rises.</headline>
<dateline>ZEELAND, Mich. 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Herman Miller, Inc.</p>
<p>			 Condensed Consolidated Statements</p>
<p>	   (Unaudited) (Dollars in 000s, except per share data)</p>
<p>						     Three Months Ended</p>
<p>						     Mar 1,	  Mar 2,</p>
<p>							 1997	   1996</p>
<p> Net Sales				     $365,060	$312,915</p>
<p> Cost of Goods Sold			   233,127	 209,500</p>
<p> Gross Margin				   131,933	 103,415</p>
<p> Operating Expenses			    96,271	  83,401</p>
<p> Restructuring/Other			   13,736		 -</p>
<p> Operating Income				21,926	  20,014</p>
<p> Other Expenses				     591	   1,369</p>
<p> Income Before Taxes			   21,335	  18,645</p>
<p> Taxes on Income				  7,800	   6,745</p>
<p> Net Income				   13,535(a)	  11,900</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share			  .56(a)	     .47</p>
<p> Common Share Equivalents		24,052,179    25,395,463</p>
<p>(a) Includes $13.7 million pretax restructuring charge which decreased net income by $5.4 million, or $.23 per share.  </p>
<p>							Nine Months Ended</p>
<p>						     Mar 1,	  Mar 2,</p>
<p>							 1997	   1996</p>
<p> Net Sales				   $1,084,681	$942,396</p>
<p> Cost of Goods Sold			   700,176	 623,449</p>
<p> Gross Margin				   384,505	 318,947</p>
<p> Operating Expenses			   284,883	 252,740</p>
<p> Patent Litigation Settlements/Other     19,236	  16,515</p>
<p> Operating Income				80,386	  49,692</p>
<p> Other Expenses				   3,753	   3,623</p>
<p> Income Before Taxes			   76,633	  46,069</p>
<p> Taxes on Income				 29,660	  17,200</p>
<p> Net Income				  46,973 (a)     28,869(b)</p>
<p> Net Income Per Share			1.95 (a)	 1.15(b)</p>
<p> Common Share Equivalents		24,127,898    25,173,703</p>
<p>(a) Includes $19.2 million pretax write-offs for restructuring of the company's German subsidiary, which decreased net income by $9.9 million, or $0.42 per share.</p>
<p>(b) Includes $16.5 million pretax litigation settlements, which decreased net income by $10.6 million, or $0.42 per share.</p>
